      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Anhrathe Fleet" hidden="false" id="f4c2-bce5-4fc1-44d8">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3ffb-5d6b-4040-b790" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Anhrathe Pirate Fleets" hidden="false" id="6229-98b6-4e89-d141" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Snatch the Prize" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="360f-7e24-9262-cc3c">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Trigger: an enemy unit ends a Movement phase move within 6" of an objective marker and within 12" of a friendly unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule. The reacting unit may immediately make a Run move. This move must end closer to that objective marker than where it began. If the reacting unit ends this move within 3" of the objective marker, it gains Feel No Pain (6+) until the start of its controlling player's next turn.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Lords of Plunder" id="4026-0de3-d3aa-e60d" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Anhrathe have spent millennia perfecting the art of taking what belongs to others. Whenever a unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule destroys an enemy unit, captures an objective marker, or causes an enemy unit to Fall Back, choose a friendly unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule within 12". That unit gains either Fleet (2), Hit &amp; Run, Precision Shots (5+) or Precision Strikes (5+) until the start of its controlling player's next turn. A unit may only benefit from Lords of Plunder once per turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Anhrathe Raiders" hidden="false" id="62a9-1ea7-017a-49cf" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Hit and Fade" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="7886-d4cd-b73f-07e9">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: an enemy unit declares a Shooting Attack targeting a friendly unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule. The reacting unit may immediately make a Run move. If the unit ends this move entirely out of range or line of sight of all weapons being used by the attacking unit, the attack is lost and has no effect. If the attacking unit can still draw line of sight and is within range after this move is completed, resolve the attack normally.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Raiders of the Void" id="fbdf-6cb4-c096-0250" hidden="false">
                  <description>Friendly units with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule gain +1 to Reserve Rolls. In addition, attacks made by units with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule against enemy units that arrived from Reserves this turn, are Falling Back, are Pinned, or are within 6" of an objective marker gain Precision Shots (6+) and Precision Strikes (6+).</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </selectionEntries>
