    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Channeller Stones" hidden="false" id="4e1f-5746-1ded-6ad0" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Channeller Stones" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1263-063a-f738-24be">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with channeller stones gains Feel No Pain (5+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Corsair Banner" hidden="false" id="0b98-5033-e3ae-965d" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Corsair Banner" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="8d49-31cd-4fb0-0f9a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Friendly Aeldari (Anhrathe) units within 6" of one or more models equipped with a Corsair banner gain +1 Leadership and Feel No Pain (6+). This Feel No Pain roll does not stack with other Feel No Pain rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Corsair Jet Pack" hidden="false" id="a6b9-3b55-f896-644a" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Corsair Jet Pack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d8de-987a-b14a-f707">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit entirely equipped with Corsair jet packs may choose to increase its Movement Characteristic by +6, move over friendly and enemy models/units, and ignore terrain while moving during the Movement phase. A unit that ends or begins its movement in Dangerous Terrain will still need to take Dangerous Terrain tests as normal, even when employing Corsair jet packs, and treats Difficult Terrain as Dangerous Terrain. In addition to the bonus to move during the Movement phase, a unit equipped entirely with Corsair jet packs may make an additional move of 6" during the Shooting phase. This move must be taken after the unit has completed any Shooting, is not limited by the weapons fired by that unit during the Shooting phase, and ignores terrain and may move over friendly and enemy models/units in the same manner as moves made using a Corsair jet pack in the Movement phase. Any model equipped with a Corsair jet pack also gains the Bulky (2) and Deep Strike special rules, or if it already has the Bulky (2) special rule it gains the Bulky (3) special rule instead. During any Reaction that allows a unit equipped entirely with Corsair jet packs to move, increase the distance of that move by 6. This allows the unit to ignore terrain in the same manner as other Corsair jet pack moves.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Faolchú" hidden="false" id="2130-ff42-defc-1a87" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Faolchú" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="78d8-c6f1-4f81-7274">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a Faolchú gains Shrouded (5+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Mistshield" hidden="false" id="374a-3177-dd5f-e812" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mistshield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="3864-84cb-9443-835e">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a mistshield gains a 5+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, models with multiple Wounds equipped with a mistshield gain Battle-hardened (1).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="4ef5-2dc2-293b-d8f0" hidden="false" targetId="1259-1608-2198-41c4" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (5+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Skyrunner Jetbike" hidden="false" id="3fd7-4a73-847d-8d8d" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Skyrunner Jetbike" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="4cc6-a475-7dc5-e23c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A Skyrunner jetbike has a twin-linked shuriken catapult. In addition, a model with a Skyrunner jetbike may choose to move up to their unmodified Initiative Characteristic at the start of the controlling player's Charge Sub-phase. A model that chooses to do so may not declare a Charge. Any model equipped with a Skyrunner jetbike must change its Unit Type to Cavalry (Antigrav) (keeping any other Unit Sub-types it previously had), change its Movement Characteristic to 18, and gains the Fleet (2), Firing Protocols (2), Hit &amp; Run, Hammer of Wrath (1), Relentless, Battle-hardened (1), Shrouded (5+), and Deep Strike special rules.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Starfang Skimmer" hidden="false" id="9be4-b5c5-51eb-b617" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Starfang Skimmer" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="bbe5-3b48-cb87-f68e">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a Starfang skimmer gains the Cavalry (Antigrav) Unit Type and has its Movement Characteristic set to 16. The model gains Hammer of Wrath (2), Fleet (2), Hit &amp; Run and Deep Strike. A model equipped with a Starfang skimmer counts as Bulky (4). A model equipped with a Starfang skimmer treats all terrain as Open Terrain during movement and may move over models and terrain freely as normal for Antigrav units. A Starfang skimmer is equipped with a disintegrator cannon and a Starfang grenade launcher.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Voidfield" hidden="false" id="3006-78d2-f352-afb1" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Voidfield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="37b5-2ee6-3e53-39b0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a voidfield gains a 4+ Invulnerable Save and Shrouded (6+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="fb86-5b57-349a-02be" hidden="false" targetId="1259-1608-2198-41c4" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (4+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Webway Harness" hidden="false" id="3ca8-d1a0-3c84-3045" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Webway Harness" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="ed69-9e47-6e01-b2d3">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with a webway harness gains the Deep Strike special rule. In addition, if every model in a unit is equipped with a webway harness, that unit may be removed from the battlefield at the end of any of its controlling player's turns if it is not locked in combat. The unit is placed into Ongoing Reserves and automatically passes all Reserve Rolls made to return to play.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Deep Strike" id="93d4-cd33-2e57-709d" hidden="false" targetId="f1e1-986f-c783-ca9e" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bladevanes" hidden="false" id="fcfa-5da6-5ae0-5b20" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bladevanes" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="33d5-c13f-c70c-a695">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Mono-molecular gravitic cutting fins mounted along the hulls of Aeldari anti-grav craft, turning the movement of the vehicle itself into a weapon.* A model equipped with bladevanes may inflict Hits against one enemy Infantry unit that it moved over during the Movement phase. That unit suffers D3 Strength 4 AP 4 Hits with Rending (6+). If the model has a Movement characteristic of 14 or greater, increase the number of Hits inflicted to D6 instead. These Hits are resolved as Shooting Attacks and may only be inflicted once per phase regardless of how many units the model moved over.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Chain-snares" hidden="false" id="0a8e-14d2-479e-f185" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Chain-snares" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="dcbd-c475-af79-b040">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Weighted mono-filament drag chains and hooked gravitic tethers mounted beneath skimmers, deployed at extreme velocity as the vehicle passes through enemy formations.* A model equipped with chain-snares may inflict Hits against one enemy Infantry unit that it moved over during the Movement phase. That unit suffers D3 Strength 5 AP - Hits with Shred and Pinning. If the model has a Movement characteristic of 14 or greater, increase the number of Hits inflicted to D6 instead. In addition, enemy units that suffer one or more unsaved Wounds from chain-snares reduce their Movement characteristic by 2 until the end of their next Turn. These Hits are resolved as Shooting Attacks and may only be inflicted once per phase regardless of how many units the model moved over.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Enhanced Aethersails" hidden="false" id="a212-8d94-9380-8d2b" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Enhanced Aethersails" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="13c3-fa5a-f5a0-06e0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Propulsion augmentation that manipulates atmospheric density and localized gravitic shear to generate extreme acceleration and evasive manoeuvring.* A model equipped with enhanced aethersails increases its Movement characteristic by +4. After completing any movement, the model gains Shrouded (5+). This effect stacks with other sources of Shrouded but cannot improve beyond Shrouded (4+). Enhanced aethersails also allow unrestricted traversal over vertical terrain and battlefield elevation differences, treating such movement as part of standard movement resolution.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Flickerfield" hidden="false" id="bc28-2c2f-98ae-293f" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Flickerfield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="58b6-a490-5fec-8cf7">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An unstable phase-displacement shield that makes attacks resolve against non-existent positional echoes.* A model equipped with a flickerfield gains a 6+ Invulnerable Save. If the model already has an Invulnerable Save, improve it by +1 to a maximum of 4+. This improvement applies before any other modifiers unless explicitly stated otherwise.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="e034-1b4a-a89a-7b06" hidden="false" targetId="1259-1608-2198-41c4" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (6+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grisly Trophies" hidden="false" id="28ac-8c71-4e98-296c" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grisly Trophies" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="197e-0fb9-05a2-122d">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Trophies of the fallen hung from a raider's hull, broadcasting terror to all who see them.* Enemy Infantry and Cavalry units within 6" of one or more models equipped with grisly trophies suffer Fear (2). This effect is applied continuously while within range.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Night Shields" hidden="false" id="a174-b9fa-624b-25ce" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Night Shields" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="93fd-83cc-8921-e012">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Targeting degradation fields that confound ballistic computation, sensor resolution and range estimation.* Enemy units targeting a model equipped with night shields for ranged attacks treat that model as 6" further away than its actual position. In addition, any ranged attack made at over 18" is resolved as Snap Shots.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shock Prow" hidden="false" id="397a-a327-8b03-f9fc" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Shock Prow" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="c7b1-db28-e9e3-7a81">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A kinetic impact prow that turns forward velocity into catastrophic structural penetration when ramming or boarding.* A model equipped with a shock prow gains Hammer of Wrath (2). If it already has Hammer of Wrath, increase its value by +2 to a maximum of 4. In addition, Charges made by this model gain Exoshock (5+) and Breaching (6+). Shock prows also apply during any rule that generates collision-based movement impacts.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Trophy Rack" hidden="false" id="02d4-ecc1-4e1c-e371" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Trophy Rack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="0247-9cd5-1f01-f606">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Racks of trophies that broadcast fear into the minds of nearby enemies.* Enemy units within 6" of one or more models equipped with trophy racks must re-roll successful Morale tests, Pinning tests, and Fear tests.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Venom Sails" hidden="false" id="61f0-c979-4e31-c53e" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Venom Sails" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="ca34-b543-2d37-38bd">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Aerodynamic displacement sails that allow rapid repositioning and post-engagement manoeuvring.* A model equipped with venom sails gains Fleet (2). If it already has Fleet, increase its value by +1 to a maximum of 4. In addition, after completing a Charge, the model gains Hit &amp; Run until the end of the turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Webway Rift Generator" hidden="false" id="8210-0635-dca6-5003" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Webway Rift Generator" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="270f-9452-2425-f41c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A device that opens controlled breaches into the Webway for the deployment and extraction of Aeldari forces.* A model equipped with a webway rift generator gains Deep Strike. In addition, friendly units arriving from Reserves within 6" of one or more such models may re-roll Reserve rolls and Scatter dice when deploying via Deep Strike.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Plasma Grenades" hidden="false" id="2fd3-7290-f329-f3ca" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Plasma Grenades" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="70f1-cc34-c89e-3662">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit with Plasma Grenades attacks at its normal Initiative after Charging through Difficult or Dangerous Terrain, but still suffers the Charge roll penalties. In the Assault phase, a model with Plasma Grenades engaged with a Building, Fortification, Vehicle, Dreadnought, or Automata may instead inflict one automatic Str 5, AP 4 Hit with Breaching (6+) at Initiative step 1. If it does, the unit Piles In at Initiative 1, and that model may not otherwise attack or use other Hit- or Wound-inflicting rules or wargear that phase (it may still Sweeping Advance).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="c951-6c46-1611-660b" name="Plasma grenades" hidden="false" targetId="ee13-9444-767a-5018" type="profile" />
      </infoLinks>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Plasma grenades" hidden="false" id="f2a6-35eb-6356-053e" type="selectionEntry" targetId="afe5-c031-49ad-c675">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8ae2-f9bc-8f43-d404" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="cbf0-38ba-5fc0-5f6a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Protect" hidden="false" id="ebcb-99b4-dbc8-9a7b" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Protect" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="3110-b7dd-eff4-3fb5">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">*The Psyker surrounds nearby allies with shimmering barriers of psychic force that bend aside incoming attacks and reinforce failing armor.* Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Psyker with this Psychic Power may select a single friendly unit within 12". That unit gains a 6+ Invulnerable Save until the end of the current player turn. When using this power, the controlling player may choose to have the Psyker take a Psychic check. If the Check is passed, then the target unit instead gains a 4+ Invulnerable Save until the end of the current player turn. If the Check is failed, then the target unit gains no benefit and the Psyker suffers Perils of the Warp.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Jinx" hidden="false" id="f04e-78f1-724a-fd17" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Jinx" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="1423-886a-7c92-0bc0">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">*The Psyker tears apart the protective fate-threads surrounding their enemies, leaving them exposed and vulnerable to incoming attacks.* Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Psyker with this Psychic Power may select a single enemy unit within 18". That unit reduces all Armour Saves, Cover Saves and Invulnerable Saves by -1 until the start of the controlling player's next turn. When using this power, the controlling player may choose to have the Psyker take a Psychic check. If the Check is passed, then the target unit instead reduces all Armour Saves, Cover Saves and Invulnerable Saves by -2 until the start of the controlling player's next turn. If the Check is failed, then the target unit suffers no additional effect and the Psyker suffers Perils of the Warp.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Guide" hidden="false" id="e58a-1447-25c5-3d97" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Guide" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="f91d-fe5a-7172-64aa">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">*The Psyker manipulates the strands of fate to guide allied warriors toward deadly precision and impossible accuracy.* Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Psyker with this Psychic Power may select a single friendly unit within 24". Until the start of the Psyker's next Psychic phase, that unit re-rolls all failed To Hit rolls with its ranged Shooting Attacks, as if its ranged weapons were Twin-linked.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Song of the Endless Void" hidden="false" id="253d-52d1-0024-3ef1" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Song of the Endless Void" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="753e-283e-cad0-2bee">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">*The Voidsinger bends perception and motion, allowing allies to flow through battle like drifting shadows between stars.* Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Psyker with this Psychic Power may select a single friendly unit within 6". That unit gains Shrouded (6+) until the end of the current player turn. Friendly Aeldari (Anhrathe) units instead gain Shrouded (4+) until the end of the current player turn. When using this power, the controlling player may choose to have the Psyker take a Psychic check. If the Check is passed, then the target unit also gains Hit &amp; Run until the end of the current player turn. If the Check is failed, then the target unit gains no benefit and the Psyker suffers Perils of the Warp.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Runes of Battle" hidden="false" id="ae62-708e-9b40-afe2" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Runes of Battle: Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="9be9-067e-e962-17bf">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4cd8-f58f-14df-023d" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="b56b-eb65-dfdc-0a8d" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <entryLinks>
            <entryLink import="true" name="Protect" hidden="false" id="e0fd-ac98-0ef3-c969" type="selectionEntry" targetId="ebcb-99b4-dbc8-9a7b">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="5d79-a066-7eea-f472" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
            </entryLink>
            <entryLink import="true" name="Jinx" hidden="false" id="e811-f32b-3638-cc43" type="selectionEntry" targetId="f04e-78f1-724a-fd17">
