          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c78b-a203-e6ca-1288" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Pirate King" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="5bba-4445-408d-565e">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord is a feared corsair lord whose reputation for greed, cunning and audacity has attracted countless followers eager to share in the spoils of war. The Warlord gains Precision Shots (4+) and Precision Strikes (4+). In addition, whenever the Warlord or a unit joined by the Warlord destroys an enemy unit, choose a friendly unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule within 12". That unit gains Feel No Pain (6+) until the start of its controlling player's next turn. If the chosen unit already has Feel No Pain, improve that roll by 1 to a maximum of 4+.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="7019-0eb7-e1c9-ddc6" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Prince of a Thousand Raids" hidden="true" id="4ec5-04df-69f9-a4a6" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="62a9-1ea7-017a-49cf" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="fd27-2312-14e3-43b8" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Prince of a Thousand Raids" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="2034-ba3d-69fd-117b">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">Few Corsair Princes survive long enough to master the art of the void raid. Those that do become living legends, orchestrating strikes of breathtaking speed and precision. The Warlord gains the Scout and Hit &amp; Run special rules. If the Warlord already has either of these special rules, they instead gain +1 to all Run and Charge distances. The controlling player gains one additional Reaction during each enemy Movement phase. This additional Reaction may only be used by a unit with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="74ce-08cf-d4d4-fbe3" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aeldari (X)" id="ab83-1787-6c8b-27fc" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>The civilization keywords represent the major surviving branches of the Aeldari species. Every Aeldari unit has at least one Civilization keyword, shown as X, which determines which armies, detachments and force organizations may include that unit. These keywords work like Legion, Klan or Household affiliations in other factions. Aeldari units may only be selected in armies whose Civilization keyword matches at least one of the unit's listed Civilization keywords unless specifically stated otherwise. Units with several Civilization keywords may be selected in any army matching one or more of them: a Corsair Voidreaver unit with the keywords Anhrathe and Asuryani may be selected in either an Anhrathe army or an Asuryani army; a Harlequin Shadowseer with the Rillietann keyword may be included only in armies permitted to include Rillietann units; an Incubi unit with only the Drukhari keyword may only be selected in a Drukhari army. Unless specifically stated otherwise, Asuryani and Drukhari units may not be selected within the same Primary Detachment; Rillietann units may be included as Allied or Auxiliary units in any Aeldari army; and Anhrathe units may be selected as Primary, Allied or Auxiliary forces alongside either Asuryani or Drukhari armies.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Void" id="9b8e-8321-d1db-ecab" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>Corsair Voidreaver and Corsair Voidscarred units in an army that includes one or more Corsair Princes gain the Line Unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Outcasts and Pirates" id="a680-bf40-82b1-2220" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>Units with this Special Rule may be selected as Non-Compulsory Troops choices in either Asuryani or Drukhari Detachments. Such units do not prevent the inclusion restrictions normally applied between Asuryani and Drukhari units within the same army. They treat Asuryani and Drukhari units as Fellow Warriors.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Prince of Corsairs" id="68a6-ec09-25a4-eb63" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>Corsair Voidreaver and Corsair Voidscarred units in an army that includes one or more Corsair Princes gain the Line Unit Sub-type. In addition, models with this trait may be included in Asuryani and Drukhari detachments and count as Sworn Brothers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Reavers of the Void" id="125c-f4e5-d9a7-0cae" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>These warriors are consummate void-raiders and ambush predators, descending from hidden Webway breaches and attack craft with terrifying precision before vanishing once more into the darkness between stars. A unit with this Special Rule gains a +1 bonus to all Reserve Rolls made to bring the unit into play from Reserves. In addition, units with this special rule may declare a Charge in a turn in which they Run in turns when they arrive from Reserves. Models with this special rule do not add their Fleet value to Charge rolls made during a turn in which they Ran.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of Dreams" id="67b1-1a86-4b4d-953a" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>A Void Dreamer may select powers from two Psychic Disciplines. One of these Disciplines must be the Voidsong Discipline.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wayfinder" id="1e2d-3572-b61c-822b" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>Friendly units with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule within 6" of one or more Way Seekers gain the Scout special rule. In addition, while a Way Seeker is on the battlefield, friendly units with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule gain +1 to Reserve Rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul Tear" id="e723-3800-b3ef-5f32" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>A unit including a Psyker and a weapon or ability with this rule may activate it before attacking with that weapon or resolving that ability, by making a single Psychic check with any Psyker in the unit. - Pass: for that phase, attacks with Soul Tear gain Armourbane (Melee), Armourbane (Ranged), and Fleshbane, and count as having Force for any rule affected by it. - Fail: no benefit, but the unit attacks as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Anhrathe Fleet (X)" id="2eda-c7d6-369b-b58f" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>An Anhrathe army may choose whether it is a Pirate Fleet or a Raider fleet; other Aeldari armies take neither. The choice gives its Civilization Trait, Advanced Reaction and Warlord Trait to units with the Aeldari (Anhrathe) special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="1259-1608-2198-41c4" hidden="false" publicationId="a8f3-52ed-030f-1805">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
